This product is derived from and inspired by the design of:

  IFEval (Instruction-Following Eval)
  Part of the Google Research repository
  https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/instruction_following_eval
  Copyright 2023 The Google Research Authors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

The following aspects of J-MeetEval derive from IFEval:

  - The instruction registry pattern used to map instruction identifiers to
    verifiable checker classes (jmeeteval/core/meeting_instructions_registry.py,
    jmeeteval/core/meeting_instructions.py)
  - The prompt-level / instruction-level strict accuracy metric definitions
    (jmeeteval/evaluation/meeting_evaluation_lib.py)
  - The overall structure of the generate-then-evaluate pipeline

J-MeetEval adapts these ideas to Japanese meeting-related tasks and adds
LLM-as-a-Judge based checkers for instructions that cannot be verified
programmatically. The implementation is an independent work and does not
copy IFEval source code verbatim.
